{"kind":"artifact","text":"The ui tree as main carries it, at merge commit 159293300dcf928ac4ae480a5a6bb61bcb5e5102, which landed the main-view selector work approved by codex in 5f92ee81 and ratified in c65982e7. (Records are named here by the trailing eight hex of their event id, as the artifacts at this path have been.)\n\nThe merge changed ui/src/components/TopBar.tsx and ui/test/dom.test.mjs. The Work and Activity selector no longer carries duplicate active and attention figures. Those numbers invited the selector to be read as a report on the work when it is a control for choosing a view, and they were a second place the same facts could be stated and disagree. The exact Active, Attention and Closed counts remain beside their WorkDrawer filters, which is the one place that owns them. dom.test.mjs pins the selector to two labels with no digit, and gives each filter a distinct value so a count rendered against the wrong filter fails rather than passing by coincidence.\n\nGates run at this exact merge commit in the main checkout: go vet ./..., go build ./..., the Go suite over ./internal/... and ./cmd/... with -count=1, npx tsc --noEmit in ui/, and the UI test suite. Results are in the report I gave the coordinator; the docset package was run on its own rather than beside another suite.\n\nSuccession. This retires two live predecessors at this path: 9c7ef567, the candidate at branch head 44461577, and 64976636, the artifact for merge commit 8924b4d0.\n\n9dc0be22 stays live, still deliberately, and it is worth being exact about which record that is. Its event is 02b730f92830ddaff587e21d83d143439dc0be22, so it appears in some notes as 02b730f9 by its leading eight and elsewhere as 9dc0be22 by its trailing eight; those are one record, not two, and I was handed a plan today that counted them as two and asked for both to be retired. Five pages cite it — docs/concepts/components.md, docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/serve.md, docs/reference/limits.md and docs/reference/mcp/presence.md — and they carry the full id, which is why a grep on either eight-character form finds all five. Retiring it would leave those pages resting on a withdrawn record and take the docset gate red; the guard added in ff6132ec refuses exactly that. Re-anchoring those five onto this record and then retiring it is ordinary implementing work and needs its own request.\n\nSo this path knowingly carries two live artifacts, and a reader should treat this one as what main carries.\n\nIt rests on 3b7f205d at cmd/gs, live and not stale, rather than on either record this merge retires or on the review of the merged head, so the retirements recorded next do not make it stale from birth.","body":{"commit":"159293300dcf928ac4ae480a5a6bb61bcb5e5102","path":"ui"}}